  "_comment": "Carrier-local fragment URN (§4.2), the derived evidence identity a tabular carrier can mint from columns it already stores. Every binding in the SourceFragment node is a mechanical expansion of the URN and nothing else: oa:hasSource is the percent-decoded artifact component, oa:start and oa:end are the half-open code-point offsets, rkaf:coordinateSystem and rkaf:selectorKind are fixed by the scheme, and rkaf:fragmentContentDigest is the trailing digest respelled with a colon. That is why the L0 carrier needs no fragments table — the row it would have held is derivable — and why a JSON-LD graph still carries the node: SHACL validates a graph, so a graph that cites a fragment contains it. rkaf:assignmentEvidenceScheme is what binds the cited values to the derived grammar; without the declaration the URN would be an unchecked mint."
}
